## THE DECISIONS OF THIS COMMIT (each Tuesday's default as coordinator; each a Question at the stamp)
- **D1: the widening of the read-only check admits ONE name, by name (Q1, STOP-CLASS).** At BASE `Oxpd1Read.cs`'s `ReadOnlyViolations` requires every row's operation to be in `ReadOperations` (5 names), to start with `Get`, and its action to end in `/` plus the operation (MEASURED, `Oxpd1Read.cs:92` to `:107` at BASE). The head keeps all three rules and widens the second to `IsReadName`: the name starts with `Get`, **or it is exactly `IsServiceEnabled`** (the constant `Oxpd1Catalogue.NonGetRead`). Why that one: HP's text says the service answers it while off ("When disabled, only this method, the EnableService method, and the DisableService method will be functional", `test.wsdl:502`), and it is the read the contracts README names before `EnableService`. **No other name passes:** over every operation of the seven committed bindings, the names without `Get` are 51 (MEASURED by T01), and `IsServiceEnabled` is the only one `IsReadName` admits (T01); with every one of them planted in BOTH the allowed list and a row, `ReadOnlyViolations` names every one but `IsServiceEnabled` (T02). `ExportCertificates` (step 3's read-first, a later lane) is refused here.
- **D2: an enable on a service already on writes nothing and exits 0 (Q2, STOP-CLASS).** The run prints `the Test service is already on; nothing was written and no undo is owed (this run did not turn it on)`, enters nothing in the undo list, and the screen capture can follow. A read that is refused (401, 403: exit 6, the read's own words), that faults or ends in any other way (exit 8), or whose `enabled` is not an `xs:boolean` (exit 8) writes nothing.
- **D3: the capture (Q3).** `oxpd1 read --read GetScreenCapture` saves the answer's bytes WHOLE as `<run folder>/panel.png` (a temporary file, then a move) only when the base64 text decodes and the bytes start with the 8-byte PNG signature; it prints the file name, the byte count and the SHA-256, never the bytes or the base64 text; any other shape saves nothing and exits 8. **Size cap:** the client's answer bound, `MaxAnswerBytes` (1 MiB of answer, refused whole, never cut; `Oxpd1ClientOptions.cs:103` at BASE), unchanged. **Never committed:** the run folder is refused inside a git work tree (exit 9, the landed `RunFolderRule`). The client's record `oxpd1-client.log` holds the base64 text as it holds every answer.
- **D4: the capture is a read of `oxpd1 read`, not a new verb (Q4)**: the read verb's discovery tree, pins, one-attempt rule and run folder apply unchanged; the lab's `--read` now takes the enum's names exactly (`Enum.GetNames<Oxpd1Read>().Contains`), which admits `IsServiceEnabled` and refuses a number (`1`) as the landed `Get` test did.
- **D5: a disable makes no read first** (Q5): it is the undo itself; HP's description does not say what a disable of a service that is off does (UNMEASURED).
- **D6: the Test service writes take no agent option** (a usage error, exit 2, before any folder or connection); the undo list writes the all-zero id for them, and a Test service line with another id, or an agent line with the all-zero id, is an unreadable line (fail closed).
- **D7: the adapter stub's Test service starts ON** (Q6): the landed cells K01 and K12 read every member of `Oxpd1Read` in one loop; a cell about the off state (T03) sets it off. The lab stub's starts OFF (a device: off at every boot).
- **D8: four landed literals move with the widening, nothing else of a landed cell** (Q7): `ContractTests.cs` C03 `Assert.Equal(5, Oxpd1Catalogue.Rows.Count)` to 7 and `Schemas()` gains `test.xsd`; `ClientTests.cs` K01 `Assert.Equal(5, stub.Seen.Count)` to 7; `WriteTests.cs` W01 `Assert.Equal(2, Oxpd1WriteCatalogue.Rows.Count)` to 4. Every other landed cell is unchanged (MEASURED: `checks_l1.py` and the numstat).
- **D9: the WS-Addressing default does not change** (the commission: "Q2 no (README lines only, no default change)"): the two README sentences that called the version UNMEASURED now state the M577 reading with its source (first-run seat runs R03 and R03b, RELAYED from `<project>/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-24_B2044_STATUS.md:26`).
